This project demonstrates four access patterns over a linked AI-governance
knowledge graph: a command-line interface, an HTTP API, a web UI, and direct
graph queries.

It encodes and cross-walks publicly published governance frameworks, each the
work of its own authors and carrying its own terms:

- NIST AI Risk Management Framework, NIST AI 600-1, and NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5 (National Institute of Standards and Technology)
- ISO/IEC 42001 (International Organization for Standardization)
- EU AI Act (European Union)
- FINOS AI Governance Framework (Fintech Open Source Foundation)
- IBM AI Risk Atlas (IBM)
- OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications and OWASP Machine Learning Security Top 10 (OWASP Foundation)
- SR 11-7 (Board of Governors of the Federal Reserve System)
- FFIEC IT Handbook (Federal Financial Institutions Examination Council)

The encodings under byo/ and graph/ are this project's interpretation of those
frameworks, not official representations of them. Consult each framework's own
publication for authoritative text.

This product maintains its documentation as a Linked Open Knowledge Format
(LOKF) bundle under .lokf/: https://lokf.nolan-nichols.com/specification/

LOKF is a semantic profile of the Open Knowledge Format (OKF) specification by
Google Cloud Platform:
https://github.com/GoogleCloudPlatform/knowledge-catalog/blob/main/okf/SPEC.md
